Harry! Hey!

265
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:00,469
Ooh!

266
00:16:00,493 --> 00:16:01,603
You're out of jail.

267
00:16:01,627 --> 00:16:03,038
Yeah, honey,
I can't sit in jail.

268
00:16:03,062 --> 00:16:04,273
You know I got to work.

269
00:16:04,297 --> 00:16:05,674
This is my attorney,
Ben Matlock.

270
00:16:05,698 --> 00:16:08,043
Ben, this is my assistant,
Frannie Morrissey.

271
00:16:08,067 --> 00:16:09,378
Excuse me.

272
00:16:09,402 --> 00:16:11,046
Awesome.

273
00:16:11,070 --> 00:16:13,315
Oh, I read about you.

274
00:16:13,339 --> 00:16:15,818
I don't care what you read
in the <i>National Informer.</i>

275
00:16:15,842 --> 00:16:18,053
- I don't defend gangsters.
- Oh, no.

276
00:16:18,077 --> 00:16:21,723
No, I meant the profile they
did on you in <i>Financial News.</i>

277
00:16:21,747 --> 00:16:23,859
Uh, you read <i>Financial News?</i>

278
00:16:23,883 --> 00:16:25,627
How else would I
know when to go short?

279
00:16:25,651 --> 00:16:27,763
Wow! You are one
of the highest-paid

280
00:16:27,787 --> 00:16:29,097
defense lawyers in the country.

281
00:16:29,121 --> 00:16:31,967
We should compare
portfolios sometime.

282
00:16:31,991 --> 00:16:33,168
Frannie, come on.

283
00:16:33,192 --> 00:16:35,103
We got a shoot.

284
00:16:35,127 --> 00:16:37,940
An artist, but a
financial illiterate.

285
00:16:37,964 --> 00:16:40,909
Relax, Harry. Mother's coming.

286
00:16:40,933 --> 00:16:42,993
I will get the film.

287
00:16:45,238 --> 00:16:48,951
Uh, how-how-how-how long
has she been your assistant?

288
00:16:48,975 --> 00:16:51,253
Almost, uh, four years.

289
00:16:51,277 --> 00:16:52,554
Oh.

290
00:16:52,578 --> 00:16:56,859
Well, where was she, uh,
when, uh, Jackie was killed?

291
00:16:56,883 --> 00:16:58,160
Yogi's.

292
00:16:58,184 --> 00:17:00,195
It's the frozen yogurt
place down the street.

293
00:17:00,219 --> 00:17:01,830
She lives on the stuff.

294
00:17:01,854 --> 00:17:03,332
Oh.

295
00:17:03,356 --> 00:17:06,869
Uh, I want you to get me a
list of everybody who was here

296
00:17:06,893 --> 00:17:08,737
when Jackie gave
you hell that day.

297
00:17:08,761 --> 00:17:09,938
- Everybody?
- Yeah.

298
00:17:09,962 --> 00:17:11,139
And-And I need, I need

299
00:17:11,163 --> 00:17:13,208
the number of your
answering service.

300
00:17:13,232 --> 00:17:14,977
Maybe we can
figure out who set up

301
00:17:15,001 --> 00:17:16,545
that phony
rendezvous in the park.

302
00:17:16,569 --> 00:17:17,779
Okay. Frannie!

303
00:17:17,803 --> 00:17:19,414
I got a job for you.

304
00:17:19,438 --> 00:17:20,949
Yeah, yeah.

305
00:17:20,973 --> 00:17:24,653
Uh, that model that was
working with Carla the other day...

306
00:17:24,677 --> 00:17:26,421
Lauren Chadwick?

307
00:17:26,445 --> 00:17:28,257
Yeah. Is she going to
be working this afternoon?

308
00:17:28,281 --> 00:17:30,025
Yeah.

309
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:32,294
As long as she
does what she's told.

310
00:17:46,532 --> 00:17:48,143
Ms. Chadwick?

311
00:17:48,167 --> 00:17:49,811
Hi. I'm Michelle Thomas.

312
00:17:49,835 --> 00:17:52,080
I'm one of Harry
Samuels' attorneys.

313
00:17:52,104 --> 00:17:54,216
Do you mind if I ask
you a few questions?

314
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:55,918
Do you work in a courtroom?

315
00:17:55,942 --> 00:17:58,220
- Sometimes.
- Well, how would you like it

316
00:17:58,244 --> 00:18:00,889
if I came down to the courthouse
and asked you a few questions

317
00:18:00,913 --> 00:18:02,541
while you were
addressing the jury?

318
00:18:03,583 --> 00:18:05,127
- I can wait.
- This is my work.

319
00:18:05,151 --> 00:18:06,995
Christie Brinkley
doesn't put up with this.

320
00:18:07,019 --> 00:18:08,630
Why should I?

321
00:18:08,654 --> 00:18:09,765
This isn't convenient.

322
00:18:09,789 --> 00:18:11,667
- I'll just come back later.
- No.

323
00:18:11,691 --> 00:18:13,402
Later is no more
convenient than now.

324
00:18:13,426 --> 00:18:15,070
Ask your questions.

325
00:18:15,094 --> 00:18:16,426
Fast.

326
00:18:17,897 --> 00:18:20,909
What happened the afternoon
of Jackie Whitman's murder?

327
00:18:20,933 --> 00:18:24,079
Jackie stormed in before
1:00, read Harry the riot act,

328
00:18:24,103 --> 00:18:26,415
trashed the makeup room
and stormed out again.

329
00:18:26,439 --> 00:18:29,117
Harry called a break, and
everyone went to lunch.

330
00:18:29,141 --> 00:18:31,420
I got back around 3:00.

331
00:18:31,444 --> 00:18:32,521
Jackie was dead.

332
00:18:32,545 --> 00:18:33,622
That's it.

333
00:18:33,646 --> 00:18:35,324
Everybody went to lunch?

334
00:18:35,348 --> 00:18:37,459
As far as I know.

335
00:18:37,483 --> 00:18:40,228
I went back to the hotel and
had some fruit in my room.

336
00:18:40,252 --> 00:18:42,431
- I don't do lunch.
- Lauren?

337
00:18:42,455 --> 00:18:44,299
Your agent.

338
00:18:44,323 --> 00:18:46,602
I'll get back to her.

339
00:18:46,626 --> 00:18:48,870
I thought Jackie
Whitman was your agent.

340
00:18:48,894 --> 00:18:50,739
Oh, she was. I outgrew her.

341
00:18:50,763 --> 00:18:53,375
I signed with a new
agent three weeks ago.

342
00:18:53,399 --> 00:18:55,243
So you and Jackie
weren't getting along.

343
00:18:55,267 --> 00:18:56,778
We got along fine.

344
00:18:56,802 --> 00:18:58,246
This was business.

345
00:18:58,270 --> 00:18:59,982
Jackie thought small.

346
00:19:00,006 --> 00:19:02,317
She wanted me
to continue doing...

347
00:19:02,341 --> 00:19:04,920
this kind of work forever.

348
00:19:04,944 --> 00:19:07,823
Miss Thomas, I'm an actress.

349
00:19:07,847 --> 00:19:09,324
I'm going to be a star.

350
00:19:09,348 --> 00:19:10,626
Lauren, come on.

351
00:19:10,650 --> 00:19:11,627
Let's go.

352
00:19:11,651 --> 00:19:13,762
Ready.

353
00:19:13,786 --> 00:19:17,065
I did not kill Jackie,
I don't know who did,

354
00:19:17,089 --> 00:19:19,422
and frankly, I don't care.

355
00:19:20,459 --> 00:19:22,360
I can see that.

356
00:19:36,208 --> 00:19:38,200
What are you doing here?

357
00:19:40,913 --> 00:19:43,325
Looking for Carla Royce.

358
00:19:43,349 --> 00:19:45,293
You seen her?

359
00:19:45,317 --> 00:19:46,695
Okay.

360
00:19:46,719 --> 00:19:48,730
This is the real me, Conrad.

361
00:19:48,754 --> 00:19:54,870
No makeup, dirty
hair and sweaty.

362
00:19:56,562 --> 00:19:59,508
Come on in, if
you still want to.

363
00:19:59,532 --> 00:20:01,543
You kidding? I know
women who would kill

364
00:20:01,567 --> 00:20:03,745
to look like you do right now.

365
00:20:03,769 --> 00:20:05,280
What you been up to?

366
00:20:05,304 --> 00:20:07,282
Well, went to the health club.

367
00:20:07,306 --> 00:20:09,985
Rode the bike for 40 minutes.

368
00:20:10,009 --> 00:20:12,421
I thought swimming
was your thing.

369
00:20:12,445 --> 00:20:14,923
Cross-training is my thing.

370
00:20:14,947 --> 00:20:17,974
Whatever keeps me in a size six.

371
00:20:19,185 --> 00:20:20,562
Mmm.

372
00:20:20,586 --> 00:20:21,763
Harry's out on bail.

373
00:20:21,787 --> 00:20:23,298
Yeah, I know. He's back at work.

374
00:20:23,322 --> 00:20:25,600
I'm supposed to be there.

375
00:20:25,624 --> 00:20:26,902
I'll drive you.

376
00:20:26,926 --> 00:20:28,804
You're a sweetheart.

377
00:20:28,828 --> 00:20:31,139
Well, I want to stay close,

378
00:20:31,163 --> 00:20:33,108
just in case it
comes time for my,

379
00:20:33,132 --> 00:20:34,710
- you knows...
- Time for what?

380
00:20:34,734 --> 00:20:36,078
You know what.

381
00:20:36,102 --> 00:20:37,979
Oh, yeah.

382
00:20:38,003 --> 00:20:39,614
Our propers.

383
00:20:39,638 --> 00:20:40,949
Right.

384
00:20:40,973 --> 00:20:43,485
And I need to talk
to Bobby Michaelson.

385
00:20:43,509 --> 00:20:44,853
You know him pretty well?

386
00:20:44,877 --> 00:20:47,108
Uh, he was Jackie's partner.

387
00:20:48,714 --> 00:20:51,526
Was their relationship more
than business, you think?

388
00:20:51,550 --> 00:20:54,362
Uh, they fought
like cats and dogs.

389
00:20:54,386 --> 00:20:58,100
Of course, being Jackie's
partner couldn't be easy.

390
00:20:58,124 --> 00:21:01,036
It's tough enough
being one of her models.

391
00:21:01,060 --> 00:21:03,138
Why do you say that?

392
00:21:03,162 --> 00:21:05,340
Well, she was a control freak.

393
00:21:05,364 --> 00:21:09,044
Parties I went to,
clothes I wore...

394
00:21:09,068 --> 00:21:11,713
jobs I took.

395
00:21:11,737 --> 00:21:14,349
She insisted on having
the last word on everything.

396
00:21:14,373 --> 00:21:16,351
It was infuriating.

397
00:21:16,375 --> 00:21:18,653
Well, why'd you put up with it?

398
00:21:18,677 --> 00:21:23,391
Because, nine times out of
ten, she was absolutely right.

399
00:21:23,415 --> 00:21:28,697
See, I was nothing when
I started with her, Conrad.

400
00:21:28,721 --> 00:21:30,398
My sister and I were literally

401
00:21:30,422 --> 00:21:32,868
on our way to the
unemployment office

402
00:21:32,892 --> 00:21:35,137
when Jackie
pulled up in this cab

403
00:21:35,161 --> 00:21:39,775
and talked us into going
with her to a studio session.

404
00:21:39,799 --> 00:21:41,710
Next thing I knew,
we were right smack

405
00:21:41,734 --> 00:21:44,012
in the middle of <i>Vogue</i> magazine.

406
00:21:44,036 --> 00:21:47,415
Lady knows what she's
doing, that's for sure.

407
00:21:47,439 --> 00:21:50,552
You didn't tell me you had a
sister who was a model, too.

408
00:21:50,576 --> 00:21:51,887
Used to be.

409
00:21:51,911 --> 00:21:54,073
She's not anymore.

410
00:21:57,917 --> 00:22:00,045
Let's go.

411
00:22:06,392 --> 00:22:07,702
Mr. Matlock.

412
00:22:07,726 --> 00:22:09,204
- Hi.
- Oh, hi, Frannie.

413
00:22:09,228 --> 00:22:11,072
Harry asked me to
run this over to you.

414
00:22:11,096 --> 00:22:12,462
- Oh...
- It's his list.

415
00:22:13,566 --> 00:22:17,679
Well, gee, you did a...
you did a neat job, Frannie.

416
00:22:17,703 --> 00:22:19,414
I was just going for a hot dog.

417
00:22:19,438 --> 00:22:20,549
Want one?

418
00:22:20,573 --> 00:22:21,650
Are you kidding?

419
00:22:21,674 --> 00:22:22,951
Hey, Charlie.

420
00:22:22,975 --> 00:22:25,187
- One hot dog all the way.
- You got it!

421
00:22:25,211 --> 00:22:26,922
You may as well
just pump cholesterol

422
00:22:26,946 --> 00:22:28,323
straight into your arteries.

423
00:22:28,347 --> 00:22:30,325
Besides, I just
came from Yogi's.

424
00:22:30,349 --> 00:22:32,627
I'm addicted to their
nonfat raspberry.

425
00:22:32,651 --> 00:22:33,795
Yeah, I know.

426
00:22:33,819 --> 00:22:34,930
I called the manager.

427
00:22:34,954 --> 00:22:37,132
He said you were in
twice on Wednesday.

428
00:22:37,156 --> 00:22:38,567
Well, yeah, after
they took Harry away,

429
00:22:38,591 --> 00:22:40,569
I just had to go in there
and calm myself down.

430
00:22:40,593 --> 00:22:41,736
Yeah.

431
00:22:41,760 --> 00:22:43,338
You checked me out?

432
00:22:43,362 --> 00:22:45,040
As a murder suspect?

433
00:22:45,064 --> 00:22:47,226
- I think I'm flattered.
- Here you are, Ben.

434
00:22:48,267 --> 00:22:50,812
You're not a suspect anymore.

435
00:22:50,836 --> 00:22:53,048
That's gross.

436
00:22:53,072 --> 00:22:55,517
So, who else are
you investigating?

437
00:22:55,541 --> 00:22:56,885
Lauren Chadwick.

438
00:22:56,909 --> 00:22:58,253
Smart move.

439
00:22:58,277 --> 00:23:01,256
She is a
mean-spirited B-I-T-C...

440
00:23:01,280 --> 00:23:03,358
- That's what my associate said.
- Mm-hmm.

441
00:23:03,382 --> 00:23:06,127
But sh-she didn't have a motive.

442
00:23:06,151 --> 00:23:08,396
And she was in her
hotel room at the time.

443
00:23:08,420 --> 00:23:09,698
No, she wasn't.

444
00:23:09,722 --> 00:23:11,333
I called her from the
yogurt shop twice.

445
00:23:11,357 --> 00:23:12,734
She took one of our dresses.

446
00:23:12,758 --> 00:23:15,971
I wanted it back, but she
wasn't there either time.

447
00:23:15,995 --> 00:23:17,272
- Really?
- Yeah.

448
00:23:17,296 --> 00:23:19,975
And the way I hear
it, nobody, but nobody,

449
00:23:19,999 --> 00:23:21,710
ever dropped Jackie
Whitman as their agent

450
00:23:21,734 --> 00:23:23,278
and lived to tell about it.

451
00:23:23,302 --> 00:23:24,479
Nobody.

452
00:23:24,503 --> 00:23:25,971
Except Lauren Chadwick.

453
00:23:27,006 --> 00:23:28,717
Draw your own conclusions.

454
00:23:28,741 --> 00:23:30,733
I got to get back.

455
00:23:31,777 --> 00:23:34,823
I like you, Ben.

456
00:23:34,847 --> 00:23:37,025
T-bills.

457
00:23:37,049 --> 00:23:38,449
Yeah.

458
00:23:45,858 --> 00:23:47,569
Yeah, yeah, that's
great. That's great.

459
00:23:49,495 --> 00:23:50,739
Right over there.

460
00:23:50,763 --> 00:23:53,508
Okay. Spin around there.

461
00:23:53,532 --> 00:23:54,943
Come on, like you're dancing.

462
00:23:54,967 --> 00:23:57,061
Yes, like you're dancing!

463
00:24:04,543 --> 00:24:06,588
Bobby?

464
00:24:06,612 --> 00:24:08,023
How you doing?

465
00:24:08,047 --> 00:24:10,158
Okay.

466
00:24:10,182 --> 00:24:12,961
Hear you took a quick
trip to New York yesterday.

467
00:24:12,985 --> 00:24:15,921
Yeah. I had some business
I had to take care of.

468
00:24:17,256 --> 00:24:18,833
You're checking up on me.

469
00:24:18,857 --> 00:24:20,101
That's my job.

470
00:24:20,125 --> 00:24:21,469
I'm an investigator

471
00:24:21,493 --> 00:24:23,371
for the attorneys
representing Harry.

472
00:24:23,395 --> 00:24:24,906
You snoop for a living.

473
00:24:24,930 --> 00:24:26,675
Yeah.

474
00:24:26,699 --> 00:24:28,910
By the way, congratulations.

475
00:24:28,934 --> 00:24:30,145
For what?

476
00:24:30,169 --> 00:24:33,481
Last week, you owned
40% of the Whitman Agency,

477
00:24:33,505 --> 00:24:35,583
and this week,
you got it all, huh?

478
00:24:35,607 --> 00:24:36,851
Not yet, I don't.

479
00:24:36,875 --> 00:24:38,810
Isn't that why you
went to New York?

480
00:24:48,354 --> 00:24:51,066
You're saying you think
that I bought into the agency

481
00:24:51,090 --> 00:24:53,068
to kill Jackie and take it over?

482
00:24:53,092 --> 00:24:55,103
Come on!

483
00:24:55,127 --> 00:24:57,272
Actually, I think you
bought into the agency

484
00:24:57,296 --> 00:24:59,307
so that you could
chase beautiful women.

485
00:25:00,432 --> 00:25:01,456
Wouldn't you?

486
00:25:02,935 --> 00:25:05,714
Where did you go the
afternoon of the murder?

487
00:25:05,738 --> 00:25:06,715
Lunch.

488
00:25:06,739 --> 00:25:07,882
Lauren needed a ride,

489
00:25:07,906 --> 00:25:09,617
so I dropped her
off at the hotel,

490
00:25:09,641 --> 00:25:11,186
and I grabbed a bite by myself.

491
00:25:11,210 --> 00:25:12,187
Where did you go?

492
00:25:12,211 --> 00:25:14,689
Some fast food place.

493
00:25:14,713 --> 00:25:16,391
Who knows?

494
00:25:16,415 --> 00:25:18,193
- Excuse me.
- Yeah.

495
00:25:18,217 --> 00:25:19,561
It's Michelle Thomas for you.

496
00:25:19,585 --> 00:25:21,029
Thank you.

497
00:25:21,053 --> 00:25:22,453
Sorry.

498
00:25:23,856 --> 00:25:25,848
Michelle.

499
00:25:30,029 --> 00:25:31,773
All right, save the lights.

500
00:25:31,797 --> 00:25:33,789
Yeah, ditto Bobby Michaelson.

501
00:25:38,404 --> 00:25:40,396
Okay, will do.

502
00:25:41,407 --> 00:25:42,550
Here you go.

503
00:25:42,574 --> 00:25:43,837
Thank you.

504
00:27:02,020 --> 00:27:03,398
Can we turn...?

505
00:27:03,422 --> 00:27:05,500
Can we turn this off?!

506
00:27:06,692 --> 00:27:07,936
Whew!

507
00:27:07,960 --> 00:27:10,238
We're not gonna
put you on the stand.

508
00:27:10,262 --> 00:27:11,573
That's fine, Ben.

509
00:27:11,597 --> 00:27:12,774
Now, you un... you understand

510
00:27:12,798 --> 00:27:14,709
why I think it's
not a good idea.

511
00:27:14,733 --> 00:27:16,111
It makes sense to me, Ben.

512
00:27:16,135 --> 00:27:18,213
Now, if you got any
questions, ask 'em now,

513
00:27:18,237 --> 00:27:19,848
because I won't be here
tomorrow, remember?

514
00:27:19,872 --> 00:27:21,249
Ben, you have
already explained it!

515
00:27:21,273 --> 00:27:22,550
Ben.

516
00:27:22,574 --> 00:27:26,187
I got it. I got it. I got it.
I got it. I got it. I got it.

517
00:27:26,211 --> 00:27:29,306
Frannie? Frannie!

518
00:27:31,049 --> 00:27:32,393
All right, check
over these proofs

519
00:27:32,417 --> 00:27:34,262
and the ones I'm still
working on in there

520
00:27:34,286 --> 00:27:36,131
and get ready to send
them to New York.

521
00:27:36,155 --> 00:27:37,398
- Okay.
- And while you're at it,

522
00:27:37,422 --> 00:27:39,701
uh, there's something you
need to show Mr. Matlock.

523
00:27:39,725 --> 00:27:41,387
- You mean the door?
- That's right.

524
00:27:47,132 --> 00:27:48,476
Don't worry about Harry.

525
00:27:48,500 --> 00:27:50,411
He's just a little uptight
about this assignment.

526
00:27:50,435 --> 00:27:51,679
It's got to be solid.

527
00:27:51,703 --> 00:27:53,581
Doesn't want anyone
saying he's lost it.

528
00:27:53,605 --> 00:27:54,749
Mm.

529
00:27:54,773 --> 00:27:56,951
Are-Are those the proofs
from the shoot today?

530
00:27:56,975 --> 00:27:58,553
Oh, yeah. Here, take a look.

531
00:27:58,577 --> 00:28:00,522
Oh, here... use this.

532
00:28:00,546 --> 00:28:01,546
Thank you.

533
00:28:02,781 --> 00:28:04,893
Ooh.

534
00:28:04,917 --> 00:28:07,195
Boy, that Lauren is
a beauty, isn't she?

535
00:28:07,219 --> 00:28:08,596
Uh-huh. So's Carla.

536
00:28:08,620 --> 00:28:10,865
Oh, yeah.

537
00:28:10,889 --> 00:28:12,734
Oh, look at Carla's smile.

538
00:28:12,758 --> 00:28:13,902
And poise.

539
00:28:13,926 --> 00:28:15,470
She's a born model.

540
00:28:15,494 --> 00:28:16,905
I know.

541
00:28:16,929 --> 00:28:18,940
So was her sister.

542
00:28:18,964 --> 00:28:20,875
Sister?

543
00:28:20,899 --> 00:28:21,876
Mm-hmm.

544
00:28:21,900 --> 00:28:23,144
Her name was Monica.

545
00:28:23,168 --> 00:28:25,680
We're talking major good looks.

546
00:28:25,704 --> 00:28:28,449
Once she and Carla started
working, they never stopped.

547
00:28:28,473 --> 00:28:30,704
Only Monica couldn't
handle the life.

548
00:28:31,977 --> 00:28:33,488
Drugs?

549
00:28:33,512 --> 00:28:36,457
Oh, yeah, in a big way.

550
00:28:36,481 --> 00:28:37,892
She dropped out
about a year ago.

551
00:28:37,916 --> 00:28:39,861
And the next thing we
heard, she was dead.

552
00:28:39,885 --> 00:28:41,729
It was a... mm... Car
accident or something.

553
00:28:41,753 --> 00:28:45,133
And then Carla stopped working
for a month or two after that.

554
00:28:45,157 --> 00:28:47,902
But when she came back,
she was really determined.

555
00:28:47,926 --> 00:28:50,004
Almost... driven.

556
00:28:50,028 --> 00:28:52,040
She hasn't stopped since.

557
00:28:52,064 --> 00:28:54,676
Monica. Who-Who-Who
was her agent?

558
00:28:54,700 --> 00:28:56,311
Same as Carla's.

559
00:28:56,335 --> 00:28:58,327
Jackie Whitman.

560
00:29:02,441 --> 00:29:04,419
<i>Do you happen to recall</i>

561
00:29:04,443 --> 00:29:06,654
what time it was when
you delivered the film

562
00:29:06,678 --> 00:29:07,922
to the studio?

563
00:29:07,946 --> 00:29:10,858
Yes. I wrote it down
on my work sheet.

564
00:29:10,882 --> 00:29:14,796
I delivered it at 1352.

565
00:29:14,820 --> 00:29:16,931
Eight minutes of
2:00 in the afternoon.

566
00:29:16,955 --> 00:29:18,900
And was Mr. Samuels
there when you arrived?

567
00:29:18,924 --> 00:29:20,635
Yes, he was in the darkroom.

568
00:29:20,659 --> 00:29:22,203
How do you know that?

569
00:29:22,227 --> 00:29:26,074
Well, the red warning light
above the door was on, and

570
00:29:26,098 --> 00:29:27,842
the stereo was
turned up full blast.

571
00:29:27,866 --> 00:29:30,211
Mr. Samuels always
turns the stereo up full blast

572
00:29:30,235 --> 00:29:31,512
when he's in the darkroom.

573
00:29:31,536 --> 00:29:33,448
Now this is very important,

574
00:29:33,472 --> 00:29:35,717
because we already
know from the cabdriver

575
00:29:35,741 --> 00:29:38,119
that the victim was
dropped off at the studio

576
00:29:38,143 --> 00:29:40,688
shortly after 2:00.

577
00:29:40,712 --> 00:29:44,692
So, is there any doubt in
your mind that Harry Samuels

578
00:29:44,716 --> 00:29:47,762
was in his studio at 1:52,

579
00:29:47,786 --> 00:29:50,465
at least ten minutes prior

580
00:29:50,489 --> 00:29:52,400
to Jackie Whitman's arrival?

581
00:29:52,424 --> 00:29:53,735
No doubts. He was there.

582
00:29:53,759 --> 00:29:55,403
Thank you.

583
00:29:55,427 --> 00:29:56,838
No further questions.

584
00:29:56,862 --> 00:29:58,172
Your witness.

585
00:29:58,196 --> 00:30:00,188
Thank you, Your Honor.

586
00:30:01,733 --> 00:30:04,612
You didn't actually <i>see</i>
Harry Samuels in the darkroom

587
00:30:04,636 --> 00:30:07,348
at any time on the afternoon
of the murder, did you?

588
00:30:07,372 --> 00:30:09,183
Well, no. I couldn't
open the door.

589
00:30:09,207 --> 00:30:10,785
I would've wrecked
whatever he was developing.

590
00:30:10,809 --> 00:30:12,787
So you're only
assuming that he was

591
00:30:12,811 --> 00:30:14,889
- in the darkroom, aren't you?
- No. It was Mr. Samuels.

592
00:30:14,913 --> 00:30:17,382
He had the stereo turned way
up, just like he always does.

593
00:30:18,950 --> 00:30:21,696
Did you say anything at the time
when you dropped off the film?

594
00:30:21,720 --> 00:30:24,799
Yeah. I said I was gonna leave
the film outside by the door.

595
00:30:24,823 --> 00:30:26,934
And did you hear anything
in response to that?

596
00:30:26,958 --> 00:30:29,003
Well, the music was
so loud, I don't think he...

597
00:30:29,027 --> 00:30:30,996
Just answer yes or no, please.

598
00:30:31,997 --> 00:30:34,642
- No.
- No.

599
00:30:34,666 --> 00:30:36,511
Now, you knew Mr. Samuels

600
00:30:36,535 --> 00:30:39,047
was in the habit of
turning on the red light

601
00:30:39,071 --> 00:30:40,815
and turning up
the stereo full blast

602
00:30:40,839 --> 00:30:42,350
whenever he worked
in the darkroom.

603
00:30:42,374 --> 00:30:43,751
Don't you think

604
00:30:43,775 --> 00:30:46,321
other people might have
known about that habit, as well?

605
00:30:46,345 --> 00:30:48,256
Objection. Calls
for speculation.

606
00:30:48,280 --> 00:30:49,457
No foundation.

607
00:30:49,481 --> 00:30:51,592
Withdraw the question.

608
00:30:51,616 --> 00:30:54,662
You didn't see
Mr. Samuels in the darkroom.

609
00:30:54,686 --> 00:30:56,964
You didn't hear Mr. Samuels'
voice in the darkroom.

610
00:30:56,988 --> 00:30:59,200
So, you really
can't state for sure

611
00:30:59,224 --> 00:31:02,704
that he was in the studio at all
when you were there, can you?

612
00:31:02,728 --> 00:31:05,391
Well, no, I guess not.

613
00:31:06,798 --> 00:31:09,110
No further questions.

614
00:31:54,279 --> 00:31:56,373
Lauren Chadwick.

615
00:31:59,518 --> 00:32:00,518
Hi.

616
00:32:01,620 --> 00:32:03,631
What are doing here?

617
00:32:03,655 --> 00:32:05,333
I followed you.

618
00:32:05,357 --> 00:32:08,069
Conrad and I are firm
believers in teamwork.

619
00:32:08,093 --> 00:32:10,872
Okay, uh, you want to know

620
00:32:10,896 --> 00:32:13,274
where we were the afternoon
Jackie was murdered.

621
00:32:13,298 --> 00:32:16,277
We were here seeing Dr. Lewis.

622
00:32:16,301 --> 00:32:20,139
We have a friend who's
ex... Uh, no, Bobby.

623
00:32:23,208 --> 00:32:25,253
I have a drug problem.

624
00:32:25,277 --> 00:32:26,988
Dr. Lewis's program
is the same one

625
00:32:27,012 --> 00:32:28,456
I'm on back in New York.

626
00:32:28,480 --> 00:32:31,559
Oh? So why did you lie before?

627
00:32:31,583 --> 00:32:34,362
Oh, my new agent has
a very strict drug policy.

628
00:32:34,386 --> 00:32:37,098
No addicts, current or former.

629
00:32:37,122 --> 00:32:38,566
Unlike Jackie.

630
00:32:38,590 --> 00:32:41,202
She figured if doing
drugs kept the models

631
00:32:41,226 --> 00:32:43,504
happy and thin, it
was okay by her.

632
00:32:43,528 --> 00:32:45,306
That's why I left.

633
00:32:45,330 --> 00:32:48,743
I mean, Jackie is a little
high-pressure for me.

634
00:32:48,767 --> 00:32:49,977
And you let her go.

635
00:32:50,001 --> 00:32:51,879
She was one of your top models.

636
00:32:51,903 --> 00:32:54,896
I didn't want her to wind
up dead, like Monica Royce.

637
00:32:56,341 --> 00:32:57,618
Clinic. Good afternoon.

638
00:32:57,642 --> 00:33:01,022
If you go public with
this, it will ruin her career.

639
00:33:01,046 --> 00:33:02,356
All right. Bye-bye.

640
00:33:02,380 --> 00:33:04,125
Well, I...

641
00:33:04,149 --> 00:33:06,494
I really can't make
any promises, but, uh,

642
00:33:06,518 --> 00:33:08,496
if your story checks out,

643
00:33:08,520 --> 00:33:10,731
I don't see why
anybody has to know.

644
00:33:10,755 --> 00:33:12,747
Thank you.

645
00:33:18,763 --> 00:33:21,164
Is it all right if I
use your phone?

646
00:33:47,125 --> 00:33:48,336
Conrad.

647
00:33:48,360 --> 00:33:50,659
- Hi.
- Hi.

648
00:33:52,797 --> 00:33:54,642
- Come on in.
- Okay.

649
00:33:54,666 --> 00:33:56,844
Listen, hang on for a sec.

650
00:33:56,868 --> 00:33:59,447
I'm gonna change.

651
00:33:59,471 --> 00:34:01,415
You don't have to change for me.

652
00:34:01,439 --> 00:34:03,101
You look fine.

653
00:34:04,109 --> 00:34:05,620
How's that song go?

654
00:34:05,644 --> 00:34:09,690
"If I'd known you were
coming, I'd have... made a pie"?

655
00:34:09,714 --> 00:34:11,225
"Baked a cake."

656
00:34:12,250 --> 00:34:15,743
Well, I've never been
good at that domestic stuff.

657
00:34:16,788 --> 00:34:18,699
How'd your appointment go?

658
00:34:18,723 --> 00:34:21,269
Pretty good.

659
00:34:21,293 --> 00:34:25,094
Bobby and Lauren
both have alibis.

660
00:34:35,407 --> 00:34:37,885
Well, I guess that's
good for them, isn't it?

661
00:34:37,909 --> 00:34:39,901
Yeah.

662
00:34:45,550 --> 00:34:48,563
What is that look?

663
00:34:48,587 --> 00:34:51,666
I don't know.

664
00:34:51,690 --> 00:34:54,101
How come you never
told me about your sister?

665
00:34:54,125 --> 00:34:55,903
I did tell you about her.

666
00:34:55,927 --> 00:34:58,453
You didn't tell me she was dead.

667
00:35:00,298 --> 00:35:02,410
Well, it-it happened less

668
00:35:02,434 --> 00:35:04,078
than-than a year ago.

669
00:35:04,102 --> 00:35:06,833
I guess it's still hard
for me to talk about.

670
00:35:08,106 --> 00:35:09,904
Want a glass of wine?

671
00:35:11,042 --> 00:35:13,034
No, thanks.

672
00:35:16,615 --> 00:35:19,226
How'd it happen?

673
00:35:19,250 --> 00:35:21,242
How does it always happen?

674
00:35:23,254 --> 00:35:25,723
Sex, drugs and rock and roll.

675
00:35:27,258 --> 00:35:30,538
Drove under the influence
one too many times.

676
00:35:30,562 --> 00:35:32,861
Went off an overpass.

677
00:35:36,935 --> 00:35:39,246
I'm sure you tried to help her.

678
00:35:39,270 --> 00:35:42,138
I did everything but
lock her in her room.

679
00:35:44,042 --> 00:35:46,034
She wouldn't listen.

680
00:35:48,880 --> 00:35:51,025
As far as she was
concerned, she was fine.

681
00:35:51,049 --> 00:35:53,661
Her pusher said she was fine;

682
00:35:53,685 --> 00:35:58,650
her... her boyfriends
said she was fine.

683
00:35:59,524 --> 00:36:03,154
Did Jackie Whitman
say she was fine?

684
00:36:06,297 --> 00:36:09,443
Honey, what are you getting at?

685
00:36:09,467 --> 00:36:12,680
Carla, are you sure you
went swimming that day?

686
00:36:12,704 --> 00:36:13,781
Of course I did.

687
00:36:13,805 --> 00:36:15,797
What...?

688
00:36:22,747 --> 00:36:27,962
Listen... baby...

689
00:36:27,986 --> 00:36:32,500
Remember those propers of yours?

690
00:36:32,524 --> 00:36:36,037
Well... wouldn't this
be the proper time?

691
00:36:36,061 --> 00:36:38,053
- Ow!
- Car...

692
00:36:40,899 --> 00:36:42,877
You sure you went swimming?

693
00:36:42,901 --> 00:36:44,893
Yes!

694
00:36:45,937 --> 00:36:47,929
Yes.

695
00:36:51,509 --> 00:36:54,321
You mean after all this
time, y-you don't want to...?

696
00:36:54,345 --> 00:36:56,371
No.

697
00:37:04,589 --> 00:37:06,581
No.

698
00:37:43,194 --> 00:37:45,172
Carla was in and
out of here all day,

699
00:37:45,196 --> 00:37:47,475
so, of course, her
fingerprints were all over.

700
00:37:47,499 --> 00:37:52,012
Yeah, I found some
of Jackie's in here, too.

701
00:37:52,036 --> 00:37:55,416
Yeah, well, this is where
she blew up at Harry.

702
00:37:55,440 --> 00:37:56,717
Completely trashed the place.

703
00:37:56,741 --> 00:37:58,919
There was glass
all over the floor.

704
00:37:58,943 --> 00:38:00,221
Who cleaned it up?

705
00:38:00,245 --> 00:38:01,222
Frannie did.

706
00:38:01,246 --> 00:38:02,456
She mopped the floor

707
00:38:02,480 --> 00:38:06,026
and then she replaced
everything that Jackie broke.

708
00:38:06,050 --> 00:38:10,998
Do you mean... these...

709
00:38:11,022 --> 00:38:13,801
are all-new makeup bottles?

710
00:38:13,825 --> 00:38:15,817
Right.

711
00:38:18,062 --> 00:38:20,622
Well, what do you make of this?

712
00:38:26,204 --> 00:38:27,181
Ben.

713
00:38:27,205 --> 00:38:28,549
Yeah.

714
00:38:28,573 --> 00:38:30,565
It's over.

715
00:38:36,114 --> 00:38:37,892
<i>H-How long...</i>

716
00:38:37,916 --> 00:38:41,695
h-have you been a-a
fashion model, Ms. Royce?

717
00:38:41,719 --> 00:38:43,364
About four years.

718
00:38:43,388 --> 00:38:45,733
And your sister Monica,

719
00:38:45,757 --> 00:38:48,769
uh, started modeling about
that same time, didn't she?

720
00:38:48,793 --> 00:38:50,271
That's right.

721
00:38:50,295 --> 00:38:52,706
What happened to her?

722
00:38:52,730 --> 00:38:55,309
She died in a car
accident almost a year ago.

723
00:38:55,333 --> 00:38:56,377
Mm.

724
00:38:56,401 --> 00:38:59,046
And according to
the police report,

725
00:38:59,070 --> 00:39:02,750
she had both alcohol and
drugs in her system, didn't she?

726
00:39:02,774 --> 00:39:06,287
Like you said,
it's in the report.

727
00:39:06,311 --> 00:39:07,988
Who was her agent?

728
00:39:08,012 --> 00:39:09,256
Jackie Whitman.

729
00:39:09,280 --> 00:39:11,258
Your Honor, I object to
this line of questioning.

730
00:39:11,282 --> 00:39:12,426
Uh, Mr. Matlock,

731
00:39:12,450 --> 00:39:14,929
I assume you have
a reason for this,

732
00:39:14,953 --> 00:39:16,697
and I ask you to get to it.

733
00:39:16,721 --> 00:39:18,432
Oh, absolutely.
Thank you, Your Honor.

734
00:39:18,456 --> 00:39:20,868
Objection overruled.

735
00:39:20,892 --> 00:39:24,271
Uh, your sister Monica was
arrested once for possession

736
00:39:24,295 --> 00:39:26,207
of cocaine, wasn't she?

737
00:39:26,231 --> 00:39:27,842
What's my sister
got to do with this?

738
00:39:27,866 --> 00:39:30,477
Please answer the question.

739
00:39:30,501 --> 00:39:32,346
Yes, she was arrested.

740
00:39:32,370 --> 00:39:33,480
Was she prosecuted?

741
00:39:33,504 --> 00:39:34,748
No.

742
00:39:34,772 --> 00:39:36,417
How come?

743
00:39:36,441 --> 00:39:37,852
The charges were dropped.

744
00:39:37,876 --> 00:39:40,821
The charges were dropped?!

745
00:39:40,845 --> 00:39:44,091
That would be very
difficult to get done.

746
00:39:44,115 --> 00:39:46,293
Who got the charges dropped?

747
00:39:46,317 --> 00:39:48,562
Jackie Whitman.

748
00:39:48,586 --> 00:39:49,563
Oh.

749
00:39:49,587 --> 00:39:52,700
So Jackie Whitman knew

750
00:39:52,724 --> 00:39:54,635
your sister had a drug problem.

751
00:39:54,659 --> 00:39:57,071
Yes.

752
00:39:57,095 --> 00:39:59,473
Did she ever suggest that, uh,

753
00:39:59,497 --> 00:40:00,875
Monica go for treatment?

754
00:40:00,899 --> 00:40:02,643
No.

755
00:40:02,667 --> 00:40:05,312
Did you ever suggest
that she get treatment?

756
00:40:05,336 --> 00:40:06,714
I begged her.

757
00:40:06,738 --> 00:40:08,649
I pleaded, I even
threatened her, I...

758
00:40:08,673 --> 00:40:10,985
You did everything
you could, didn't you?

759
00:40:11,009 --> 00:40:12,987
But your sister never got help.

760
00:40:13,011 --> 00:40:15,656
Do you know why?

761
00:40:15,680 --> 00:40:17,224
No.

762
00:40:17,248 --> 00:40:20,527
Wasn't it because...

763
00:40:20,551 --> 00:40:25,332
Jackie Whitman
controlled your sister?

764
00:40:25,356 --> 00:40:27,067
She not only
controlled her career,

765
00:40:27,091 --> 00:40:29,136
she controlled her life.

766
00:40:29,160 --> 00:40:32,473
All she wanted was for
Monica to keep working.

767
00:40:32,497 --> 00:40:36,443
If it took drugs to do
that, then she didn't care.

768
00:40:36,467 --> 00:40:37,878
She had more control over your

769
00:40:37,902 --> 00:40:40,781
sister than you did,
and you hated her for it.

770
00:40:40,805 --> 00:40:43,183
And you blamed her
for your sister's death.

771
00:40:43,207 --> 00:40:44,451
- Didn't you?
- No!

772
00:40:44,475 --> 00:40:47,855
I think yes. I think you
stayed with her agency

773
00:40:47,879 --> 00:40:51,859
and just waited for
the right time and place

774
00:40:51,883 --> 00:40:53,193
to avenge your sister's death.

775
00:40:53,217 --> 00:40:55,129
That's not true.

776
00:40:55,153 --> 00:40:59,300
And when she came storming
into Harry Samuels' studio

777
00:40:59,324 --> 00:41:01,368
that day and threatened him,

778
00:41:01,392 --> 00:41:04,004
you knew your waiting was over.

779
00:41:04,028 --> 00:41:06,607
You knew you could
kill Jackie Whitman,

780
00:41:06,631 --> 00:41:09,310
and Harry Samuels would
be blamed for her murder.

781
00:41:09,334 --> 00:41:10,544
And that's just what you did.

782
00:41:10,568 --> 00:41:11,946
No.

783
00:41:11,970 --> 00:41:15,449
You took a taxicab
back to your hotel

784
00:41:15,473 --> 00:41:19,086
and lured Harry Samuels out
of his studio with one phone call.

785
00:41:19,110 --> 00:41:21,689
Then you lured Jackie
Whitman back to the studio

786
00:41:21,713 --> 00:41:23,057
with another phone call.

787
00:41:23,081 --> 00:41:27,127
Then you took a cab back
to the studio, got the scissors

788
00:41:27,151 --> 00:41:29,930
from Harry's desk, and
waited for Jackie to show up.

789
00:41:29,954 --> 00:41:31,198
No, I didn't.

790
00:41:31,222 --> 00:41:33,567
Then, when that delivery
boy showed up unexpectedly,

791
00:41:33,591 --> 00:41:35,202
you ducked into the darkroom

792
00:41:35,226 --> 00:41:38,339
and turned on the stereo
so he'd think Harry was there,

793
00:41:38,363 --> 00:41:42,209
and when the delivery
boy left and Jackie came in,

794
00:41:42,233 --> 00:41:44,945
you stayed in that darkroom.

795
00:41:44,969 --> 00:41:47,047
When Jackie walked
into that darkroom,

796
00:41:47,071 --> 00:41:49,450
you stabbed her to death
with those scissors, didn't you?

797
00:41:49,474 --> 00:41:51,018
Absolutely not!

798
00:41:51,042 --> 00:41:52,786
And then you
cleaned yourself up,

799
00:41:52,810 --> 00:41:56,190
went back to the hotel, and
acted as surprised as anyone

800
00:41:56,214 --> 00:41:57,558
when you heard she was dead.

801
00:41:57,582 --> 00:41:59,493
- No!
- Your Honor, I object.

802
00:41:59,517 --> 00:42:02,715
Mr. Matlock has yet to
offer one shred of proof.

803
00:42:04,522 --> 00:42:08,669
The proof... The proof is

804
00:42:08,693 --> 00:42:10,889
right here, Julie.

805
00:42:12,163 --> 00:42:14,508
Madam Prosecutor.

806
00:42:14,532 --> 00:42:16,910
I am showing you

807
00:42:16,934 --> 00:42:21,382
telephone records
subpoenaed from your hotel...

808
00:42:21,406 --> 00:42:24,585
all the calls you
made that afternoon.

809
00:42:24,609 --> 00:42:27,955
The proof is in
the call you made

810
00:42:27,979 --> 00:42:30,657
to Harry Samuels'
answering service at 1:10.

811
00:42:30,681 --> 00:42:33,560
I wanted to ask him how much
longer he was going to need me.

812
00:42:33,584 --> 00:42:35,562
The proof is in the call

813
00:42:35,586 --> 00:42:39,133
you made to Jackie
Whitman's room at 1:11.

814
00:42:39,157 --> 00:42:41,035
She was my agent.

815
00:42:41,059 --> 00:42:43,103
I wanted to discuss
my next booking.

816
00:42:43,127 --> 00:42:47,326
The proof is in the acid burn
that's on your lower left arm.

817
00:42:48,833 --> 00:42:51,311
Uh... I don't know what
you're talking about.

818
00:42:51,335 --> 00:42:53,447
I'm talking about the
burn you sustained

819
00:42:53,471 --> 00:42:55,849
when you stabbed Jackie Whitman.

820
00:42:55,873 --> 00:42:58,919
She fell against a counter,
knocked over a bottle of acid,

821
00:42:58,943 --> 00:43:01,255
and part of it splashed
on your arm, didn't it?

822
00:43:01,279 --> 00:43:02,256
No!

823
00:43:02,280 --> 00:43:04,458
That's why...

824
00:43:04,482 --> 00:43:07,611
during the rest of the shoot...

825
00:43:08,653 --> 00:43:10,764
you took great pains

826
00:43:10,788 --> 00:43:14,034
to hide your left
arm from the camera

827
00:43:14,058 --> 00:43:16,003
and why you were very careful

828
00:43:16,027 --> 00:43:18,939
to wear long-sleeved
blouses and dresses

829
00:43:18,963 --> 00:43:22,042
and why there was a
tube of burn medicine

830
00:43:22,066 --> 00:43:23,510
next to your bed

831
00:43:23,534 --> 00:43:26,747
and why you cried out with
pain when a certain friend

832
00:43:26,771 --> 00:43:28,949
of yours grabbed your
arm the other night.

833
00:43:28,973 --> 00:43:30,601
Didn't you?

834
00:43:32,577 --> 00:43:34,555
I have a burn

835
00:43:34,579 --> 00:43:37,658
on my arm, yes, but
it's from, from spilling

836
00:43:37,682 --> 00:43:40,994
hot coffee on it, not, not acid.

837
00:43:41,018 --> 00:43:42,996
That's an acid burn.

838
00:43:43,020 --> 00:43:47,000
You know it and I know it...

839
00:43:47,024 --> 00:43:51,724
and this police
report proves it.

840
00:43:54,499 --> 00:43:58,712
A lot of bottles of makeup
got broken that afternoon,

841
00:43:58,736 --> 00:44:01,648
during the argument between
Harry and Jackie, didn't they?

842
00:44:01,672 --> 00:44:03,150
The place was a mess.

843
00:44:03,174 --> 00:44:06,286
Yeah, and Harry's
assistant, Frannie Morrissey,

844
00:44:06,310 --> 00:44:07,354
cleaned it up.

845
00:44:07,378 --> 00:44:09,323
Also, she replaced all

846
00:44:09,347 --> 00:44:13,093
of the old makeup
bottles with new ones.

847
00:44:13,117 --> 00:44:16,230
Now, that means

848
00:44:16,254 --> 00:44:20,367
the only fingerprints that
should be on those bottles,

849
00:44:20,391 --> 00:44:25,005
when the police dusted
after the murder, were hers.

850
00:44:25,029 --> 00:44:26,840
Correct?

851
00:44:26,864 --> 00:44:28,675
I suppose.

852
00:44:28,699 --> 00:44:32,246
Would you please look at
this police report and read

853
00:44:32,270 --> 00:44:35,516
the names of the people
whose prints were found

854
00:44:35,540 --> 00:44:38,510
on one of those bottles?

855
00:44:40,545 --> 00:44:43,071
Frances Morrissey and...

856
00:44:46,417 --> 00:44:48,695
Carla Royce.

857
00:44:48,719 --> 00:44:50,864
That's you.

858
00:44:50,888 --> 00:44:53,267
If you left the studio

859
00:44:53,291 --> 00:44:56,103
before Frannie was done

860
00:44:56,127 --> 00:44:59,806
replacing all those bottles,
and didn't come back

861
00:44:59,830 --> 00:45:02,809
till the police cordoned
off the whole area,

862
00:45:02,833 --> 00:45:06,880
how did your
fingerprints get all over

863
00:45:06,904 --> 00:45:09,169
one of those brand-new bottles?

864
00:45:13,110 --> 00:45:16,274
That is an acid burn on
your arm, isn't it, Carla?

865
00:45:18,216 --> 00:45:21,795
You couldn't take a
chance of someone seeing it

866
00:45:21,819 --> 00:45:25,032
and asking questions.

867
00:45:25,056 --> 00:45:28,135
How it must have hurt

868
00:45:28,159 --> 00:45:31,738
when you took the
makeup from that bottle

869
00:45:31,762 --> 00:45:35,756
and rubbed it on
that acid burn, hmm?

870
00:45:42,039 --> 00:45:46,186
I refuse to answer
any more questions

871
00:45:46,210 --> 00:45:48,270
until I see an attorney.

872
00:45:54,518 --> 00:45:56,419
No further questions.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
